"# Figure description: `fig_intercept_error`\n\n**Title:** Recorded Mean Squared Error for Three Intercept Corrections\n\n## Data and variable mapping\n\nThe plot shows exactly three recorded observations from the experimental log. No other points, curves, or intervals are drawn.\n\n| Point | b (x-axis) | MSE (y-axis) | Label |\n|---:|---:|---:|---|\n| 1 | 0 | 9 | \"(0, 9)\" |\n| 2 | 1.5 | 2.25 | \"(1.5, 2.25)\" |\n| 3 | 3 | 0 | \"(3, 0)\" |\n\n- **x channel:** `b`, the added intercept correction. Values are 0, 1.5, and 3.\n- **y channel:** `MSE`, the mean squared error. Values are 9, 2.25, and 0.\n- **hue / shape / size:** A single series. All points share one fill and one marker shape, so no legend is needed.\n\n**Supporting arithmetic (not plotted):** The five observations are (x, y) = (-2, -1), (-1, 1), (0, 3), (1, 5), (2, 7). The residuals y \u2212 2x are all 3, so the correction is b = mean(y \u2212 2x) = 3. For each candidate b, the errors y \u2212 (2x + b) are 3, 1.5, and 0 respectively, which give the MAE and MSE values in the table above. The MAE values (3, 1.5, 0) are not plotted.\n\n## Presentation\n\n**Canvas and theme**\n- Figure size: 6.0 \u00d7 4.0 in, 300 dpi.\n- Theme: `theme_minimal()` with a white background (`#FFFFFF`).\n- Panel border: none.\n- Major gridlines: horizontal only, `#E5E5E5`, 0.4 pt. Vertical major gridlines are removed. Minor gridlines are removed.\n\n**Typography**\n- Title: 14 pt, bold, `#222222`, left-aligned.\n- x-axis title: \"Added intercept correction b (unitless)\", 12 pt, `#222222`.\n- y-axis title: \"Mean squared error (MSE)\", 12 pt, `#222222`.\n- Tick labels: 10 pt, `#444444`.\n- Point labels: 10 pt, `#222222`, placed above each point.\n\n**Markers**\n- Shape 21 (filled circle with outline).\n- Fill `#1F4E79`, outline `#FFFFFF`, outline width 0.8 pt.\n- Diameter 4.5 mm (ggplot2 `size = 4.5`).\n- No connecting line. The three points are discrete and must not be joined by a curve or fit.\n\n**Axes**\n- x-axis: continuous, limits [\u22120.25, 3.25], breaks at 0, 1.5, 3, labelled \"0.0\", \"1.5\", \"3.0\".\n- y-axis: continuous, limits [0, 10], breaks at 0, 2, 4, 6, 8, 10.\n- Axis lines: 0.5 pt, `#444444`, on the left and bottom only.\n\n**Annotations**\n- Each point gets a text label offset 0.35 units above the marker.\n- Labels use the exact recorded values: \"(0, 9)\", \"(1.5, 2.25)\", \"(3, 0)\".\n- No uncertainty bars, reference curves, shaded regions, or annotations that imply generalization.\n\n**Legend:** Removed (`legend.position = \"none\"`).\n\n**Caption (optional, below the plot, 9 pt, `#666666`):**\n\"Three recorded values from a single deterministic calculation on five synthetic observations. No repetitions, optimization, or held-out evaluation.\"\n\n## Reproducibility notes\n\n- Language: R with ggplot2.\n- Data frame: `data.frame(b = c(0, 1.5, 3), mse = c(9, 2.25, 0))`.\n- Geometry: `geom_point(shape = 21, fill = \"#1F4E79\", colour = \"#FFFFFF\", size = 4.5, stroke = 0.8)` plus `geom_text(aes(label = ...), vjust = -1, size = 3.5)`.\n- Do not add `geom_line`, `geom_smooth`, or any interpolation."